      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "SECTION A: TIME, SPEED & DISTANCE"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Time, Speed & Distance covers foundational calculations including unit conversions, relative speeds, and train collision/overtaking scenarios.",
        "Basic Mensuration focuses on geometric properties, distinguishing between 2D plane figures and 3D solid structures.",
        "Data Interpretation tests the ability to analyze, calculate, and infer results from structured tables, charts, or graphs.",
        "Systematic practice through chapter questions and self-verification via the Answer Key is critical for speed and accuracy in competitive exams."
      ],
      "id": "gmzr445"
    },
    {
      "id": "w6wd3is",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "1. BASIC CONCEPT"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gp2nty0",
      "content": "Speed = Distance / Time<br></br>Distance = Speed × Time<br></br>Time = Distance / Speed<br></br><br></br>SBIquestions from this area are direct and calculation-light."
    },
    {
      "id": "g8e7loo",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "2. SPEED CONVERSION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hov07ms",
      "content": "1 km/hr = 5/18 m/s<br></br>1 m/s = 18/5 km/hr<br></br><br></br>Example:<br></br>36 km/hr = 36 × 5/18 = 10 m/s"
    },
    {
      "id": "fyeh4b6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "3. AVERAGE SPEED"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "op9adpx",
      "content": "For equal distance:<br></br>Average speed = (2xy)/(x+y)<br></br><br></br>Example:<br></br>40 km/hr and 60 km/hr<br></br>Average speed = 48 km/hr"
    },
    {
      "id": "mpx49y1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "4. RELATIVE SPEED"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "93n1zdj",
      "content": "Same direction: Difference of speeds<br></br>Opposite direction: Sum of speeds<br></br><br></br>Example:<br></br>50 km/hr and 70 km/hr (opposite)<br></br>Relative speed = 120 km/hr"
    },
    {
      "id": "0u0qns7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5. TRAIN PROBLEMS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rt6bchp",
      "content": "Time to cross an object = Length / Relative speed<br></br><br></br>Example:<br></br>Train length = 100 m, time = 10 s<br></br>Speed = 10 m/s"
    },
    {
      "id": "s402a00",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "SECTION B: BASIC MENSURATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ahduw2t",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "6. 2D FIGURES"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "x54tina",
      "content": "Square:<br></br>Area = a², Perimeter = 4a<br></br><br></br>Rectangle:<br></br>Area = l × b, Perimeter = 2(l+b)<br></br><br></br>Circle:<br></br>Area = πr², Circumference = 2πr"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1p7u0oe",
      "content": "Example:<br></br>Radius = 7 cm<br></br>Area = 154 cm²"
    },
